{
  "_comment": [
    "Dataset profiles for convert_dataset.py. Adding a dataset means adding an entry here,",
    "not editing Python: --dataset takes its choices from this file, and --profiles points at",
    "a different one (e.g. a private dataset kept outside the repo).",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  ext           input extension: .ply | .las | .laz | .txt | .npy_pair",
    "  has_rgb       whether the files carry per-point colour",
    "  rgb_max       value that means full intensity (255 for 8-bit, 1.0 if already normalized)",
    "  spatial_scale metres used to normalize the spatial-context channels; roughly the size",
    "                of the structures that matter (0.1 indoor/roadway ... 2.0 aerial)",
    "  label_field   name of the label property inside a .ply",
    "  label_map     {raw_id: contiguous_id} as strings, or null when ids are already 0..N-1",
    "  ignore        raw ids dropped before training (sentinels such as 'unclassified')",
    "  class_names   IN LABEL-ID ORDER. This is the field that silently corrupts every",
    "                per-class metric if it is written in some other order.",
    "  test_stems    file stems held out; empty means the caller picks the split",
    "  points_suffix / labels_suffix   only for the .npy_pair layout"
  ],
